A translation of CPython code
-----------------------------

    src/lib/hooks.js     in part: shlexSplit, from Lib/shlex.py
                         (shlex.read_token)

shlexSplit is a translation into JavaScript of the token state machine of
the shlex module of CPython (https://github.com/python/cpython), the
reference implementation of Python, so that this package splits a hook
command as Lazaret's Python package does. It is distributed under CPython's
license: the Python Software Foundation License Version 2 and the older
licenses of CPython's license stack, in LICENSE-PYTHON (CPython 3.14.0's
LICENSE file, unchanged; SPDX: Python-2.0.1).

    Copyright (c) 2001 Python Software Foundation; All Rights Reserved

Lib/shlex.py carries no notice of its own; CPython's license covers it.

Summary of the changes (section 3 of the PSF License):
- Translated from Python into JavaScript, as one loop over the command's
  UTF-16 code units; a run of ordinary characters is copied as a slice.
- One configuration of shlex only: posix=True, punctuation_chars=True,
  whitespace_split=True, no commenters.
- Where shlex raises ValueError (a quote left open, a backslash at the end)
  it returns null.

src/lib/codecs.js lists, in PY_CODEC_ALIASES, the codec names CPython's
encodings package resolves (encodings.aliases and its modules), under the
same license.


Unicode data
------------

    src/lib/unicode13.js   the code points Unicode 13.0 assigns
    src/lib/codecs.js      in part: SINGLE_BYTE_CODECS, the characters
                           each single-byte codec decodes bytes to

These tables are read from Python 3.10's unicodedata and from Python's
codecs, whose single-byte codecs CPython made for the most part from the
